---
import Section from '../ui/Section.astro';
import Table from '../ui/Table.astro';
---

<Section id="fits" eyebrow="Where it fits" title="Between a distro and a unikernel.">
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    Unikernels boot fast but need their own drivers and a port of every app. Distro images run everything but carry an
    OS you never use. liam keeps Linux's hardware support and drops the rest.
  </Fragment>
  <Table
    caption="liam compared with other ways to serve a site"
    columns={['', 'In the image', 'Boots as a VM in', 'Hardware support', 'Dynamic apps']}
    highlight={3}
    rows={[
      ['Distro + nginx', 'Shell, package manager, libc, init system', 'Seconds', 'Linux', 'Separate processes'],
      ['Distroless + your server', 'Your binary and libc', 'Container only', 'Host kernel', 'Your code'],
      ['Unikernel', 'One app linked with a library OS', 'Milliseconds', 'A per-project driver set', 'Ported into the image'],
      ['liam', 'Two static binaries and your site', 'Milliseconds (budget)', 'Linux LTS', 'Proxy, Wasm, or one supervised process'],
    ]}
  />
</Section>
